# The same undirected walk as explore.keys, with an orc rogue instead of an
# orc barbarian, and with searching, hiding and picking up mixed in.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/explore-rogue.keys 1
#
# Why a fourth character: the game's own class screen calls the rogue the
# character that exercises the skill system. A rogue starts with fourteen
# skill ranks against a barbarian's five, so searching, hiding and the
# stealth checks that follow the player around actually succeed sometimes
# instead of failing every roll.
#
#   s   search        h   hide in shadows        .   rest
#   >   try the stairs
#
#   g d ESC DOWN ENTER   pick up; see below for why it is five keys, not one.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING AN 'ESC'. ESC does not cancel. In play mode it
# OPENS the System Menu -- [a] Save and Quit, [b] Save and Continue, [c] Quit
# Game -- and a second ESC closes it again. A lone ESC therefore leaves that
# menu open, and while it is open ENTER means Save and Quit, because Save and
# Quit is the highlighted option. A pair of ESCs is only safe when the block
# in front of it left no menu of its own open, and a walk cannot know that.
#
# This is not a theory. Three earlier drafts of this file died of it. The
# first wrote bare ESC pairs through the walk; a 'g' over loot opened the
# container view, the pairing went out of step around block 150 of 300, and
# the last third of the run was swallowed by an open menu. The second closed
# the container view with ENTER; that worked from the container view but meant
# Save and Quit whenever the System Menu was the thing on screen instead, so
# the run saved, quit and exited 0 at block 150 -- which reads as a healthy
# session unless you look at the last screen dump. The third used
# 'g ESC DOWN ENTER', which handled both of those and still stuck on seed 42,
# because the container view REFUSES to close while an item sits in the
# In-the-Air slot, and says so.
#
# Hence 'g d ESC DOWN ENTER', the only ESC in the walk. After 'g' the screen
# is in one of two states, and these five keys land in play mode from both:
#   container view open, because 'g' found loot: 'd' drops whatever is in the
#     In-the-Air slot, ESC is then its Done key, DOWN walks a step, ENTER
#     answers 'You can't go in anything here'.
#   nothing open, because the floor was bare: 'd' shows the character sheet,
#     ESC closes it, DOWN walks a step, ENTER answers as above.
# Dropping what was just picked up sounds pointless. It is not: the pick-up,
# the encumbrance check and the drop all run, and the walk does not slow to a
# crawl under the weight of everything it has ever stood on.
#
# The System Menu itself is exercised once, in the prologue, where the state
# of the screen is known.
#
# Generated, and regenerable: a fixed seed, a weighted pool of blocks, 300 of
# them, a screen dump every 50.

@include chargen-rogue.keys

@dump:arrival

# The arrival room description is still on the screen, and it eats the first
# keystroke. Spend one on it deliberately, then open and close the System
# Menu once. This is the only place in the file where ESC is safe, because it
# is the only place where the state of the screen is known; see the note
# above. The dump proves the game came back to play mode.
SPACE
ESC ESC
@dump:sysmenu

PGDN*2 HOME*6 s s h RIGHT*5 DOWN*1 h DOWN*6
LEFT*4 h PGDN*6 PGUP*4 h RIGHT*1 PGUP*1 .*3 PGDN*3
s s > s h g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGDN*2 h PGUP*5
UP*3 .*3 HOME*5 > g d ESC DOWN ENTER g d ESC DOWN ENTER h h DOWN*5
PGDN*5 .*3 DOWN*4 h > PGUP*1 HOME*5 > PGDN*4
END*2 LEFT*3 h s PGUP*6 @dump:walk50 LEFT*4 h LEFT*3
PGUP*6 PGUP*4 g d ESC DOWN ENTER g d ESC DOWN ENTER DOWN*4 HOME*6 g d ESC DOWN ENTER > >
RIGHT*5 .*3 g d ESC DOWN ENTER DOWN*4 RIGHT*6 UP*4 HOME*1 UP*5 s
END*4 RIGHT*5 DOWN*4 s g d ESC DOWN ENTER .*3 LEFT*4 h HOME*3
g d ESC DOWN ENTER h DOWN*3 g d ESC DOWN ENTER g d ESC DOWN ENTER RIGHT*1 s PGUP*2 s
PGUP*1 HOME*2 s DOWN*1 LEFT*1 g d ESC DOWN ENTER s s PGDN*5
s LEFT*6 @dump:walk100 LEFT*1 DOWN*3 s LEFT*4 s DOWN*4
LEFT*2 UP*3 DOWN*4 UP*4 h LEFT*2 h PGUP*2 h
h PGUP*2 PGDN*3 s h PGDN*1 h s RIGHT*1
END*3 .*3 g d ESC DOWN ENTER LEFT*4 .*3 .*3 HOME*1 RIGHT*4 DOWN*1
END*5 h h g d ESC DOWN ENTER h h h PGUP*2 s
g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGUP*4 s h DOWN*3 HOME*1 g d ESC DOWN ENTER s @dump:walk150
END*4 PGDN*2 HOME*1 s h g d ESC DOWN ENTER LEFT*5 g d ESC DOWN ENTER g d ESC DOWN ENTER
UP*6 PGUP*6 h DOWN*5 END*2 h h h h
g d ESC DOWN ENTER .*3 g d ESC DOWN ENTER .*3 UP*5 h PGUP*5 END*2 LEFT*4
h PGUP*1 g d ESC DOWN ENTER HOME*1 g d ESC DOWN ENTER UP*5 .*3 UP*1 h
g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGDN*6 .*3 UP*1 s PGUP*5 PGUP*1 LEFT*4 s
g d ESC DOWN ENTER > h UP*2 s @dump:walk200 h h g d ESC DOWN ENTER
END*4 s LEFT*6 g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGUP*3 PGUP*4 h .*3 s
> s g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGDN*6 h RIGHT*1 s LEFT*2 s
s g d ESC DOWN ENTER .*3 > .*3 RIGHT*5 .*3 UP*4 s
UP*6 END*6 s HOME*5 DOWN*6 g d ESC DOWN ENTER g d ESC DOWN ENTER g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGDN*2
END*1 h g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGUP*1 HOME*4 h .*3 > UP*6
.*3 g d ESC DOWN ENTER @dump:walk250 s g d ESC DOWN ENTER PGDN*3 g d ESC DOWN ENTER DOWN*3 LEFT*6
h h RIGHT*2 DOWN*6 RIGHT*1 s PGDN*5 s HOME*2
HOME*4 > END*6 h UP*6 END*5 s HOME*2 DOWN*6
RIGHT*3 h PGUP*1 s PGUP*1 RIGHT*5 LEFT*1 h PGDN*5
UP*6 s END*4 HOME*4 s END*5 s s h
LEFT*5 g d ESC DOWN ENTER > s s DOWN*4 END*1 HOME*2

@dump:final
@quit
